issue_context.body:
The motivation of this issue is that, today, declarative schema changer does not handle the following case well
```
SET use_declarative_schema_changer = 'unsafe_always';
BEGIN;
CREATE SCHEMA sc;
DROP SCHEMA sc;
.... -- more DDL stmts
COMMIT
```

Namely, `DROP SCHEMA` will need to revert target status of elements previously added from `CREATE SCHEMA`. What makes the issue more interesting is that those elements might have transitioned from their initial status during the statementPhase of `CREATE SCHEMA` and thus had side-effects on the (in-memory) desc collection. Ideally, those sides effects need to be un-done during the statementPhase of the `CREATE SCHEMA`.



Jira issue: CRDB-28362

Epic CRDB-25313

comments:
The above PR fixes some outstanding issues but not all. At this point we have

